#edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067734 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a563e43e-1fa8-5820-bb4a-5b000405ebe0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067735 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt[3]{8x - 1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067735 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067735 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f13c9818-e5bd-5482-9a19-6a8273c58e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067736 #edb/ref 1080 "2x - 1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067736 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067736 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b0b96d9-0db2-5efe-8a1f-b20767212917" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067737 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt[3]{x} - 1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067737 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067737 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6fdf7801-387b-59b1-9efc-af9c3983c00e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068467 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068467 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $\\sqrt[3]{-8x^6}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ca53a08-7b11-552c-983f-96e7a392156c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068467 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt[3]{-8x^{6}} &=  \\\\\n\\sqrt[3]{(-2x^{2}) \\cdot (-2x^{2}) \\cdot (-2x^{2})} &=  \\\\\n\\sqrt[3]{(-2x^{2})^{3}} &=  \\\\\n&= - 2x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068468 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068468 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{\\dfrac{a^3}{(b-1)^3}}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068468 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c52719a7-544b-5844-b716-9b9d2999c028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068468 #edb/ref 1074 "We write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt[3]{(a^{3})/((b - 1)^{3})} &=  \\\\\n\\sqrt[3]{(a)/((b - 1)) \\cdot (a)/((b - 1)) \\cdot (a)/((b - 1))} &=  \\\\\n\\sqrt[3]{(\\frac{a}{b - 1})^{3}} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{a}{b - 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068639 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7223" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068639 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{(5x - 4)^3}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068639 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca60143b-d02c-5497-a134-56444304c2fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068639 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression underneath the radical is already a perfect cube. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt[3]{(5x - 4)^{3}} &= 5x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068796 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068796 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068796 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding Cube Roots of Terms Containing Binomials" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068796 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068796 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3979b4ea-910f-5037-b8e8-b0297f31c47c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Cube Root of a Monomial" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068850 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "942732a6-ca14-5b61-b8fb-ab9ef81610cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068851 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Cube Root of a Fraction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068851 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068851 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "11c07788-b01d-5788-b2f1-0a027ea53cb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1045 "The Cube Root of a Perfect Cube With Algebraic Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068929 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f64241dc-95fe-569e-8afc-913a546e0d46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069427 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186067732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069427 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069427 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{(2x - 1)^{3}}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f85c6ba2-7023-57fb-a7f0-f9cb4849e914" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069719 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069719 #edb/ref 1061 26723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069719 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "20d6dd44-7fc6-52a1-a076-27ddb6da9696" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069719 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069797 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069797 #edb/ref 1061 4295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069797 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e24a880-f9da-5e1e-b0bf-5bb2128d72a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069797 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069798 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069798 #edb/ref 1061 4296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069798 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eea06921-8121-51a7-86ad-15824cc00550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069798 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069799 #edb/ref 1061 4299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069799 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7015e37-4cd2-5ffb-814e-264ca9a0b345" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069799 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069942 #edb/ref 1064 "To find the **cube root** of a number $x$, we must ask ourselves, \"what number *cubed* equals $x$?\"\n\nFor example, the cube root of $8$ is $2$ since\n\n$$\n2^3 = 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 = 8\n$$\n\nand the cube root of $-8$ is $-2$ since\n\n$$\n(-2)^3 = (-2) \\cdot (-2) \\cdot (-2) = -8\n$$\n\nIn general, the cube root of $x^3$ is $x$.\n\nLike the square root, the cube root is signified by a radical symbol, but it also has a little $3$ next to it, i.e., $\\sqrt[3\\!\\phantom{p}]{\\phantom{2}}$. Using this notation, we can express the above statements mathematically:\n\n- \"The cube root of $8$ is $2$\" can be expressed as $\\sqrt[3]{8}=2$.\n- \"The cube root of $-8$ is $-2$\" can be expressed as $\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2$.\n- \"The cube root of $x^3$ is $x$\" can be expressed as $\\sqrt[3]{x^3}=x$.\n\n**Note:** For square roots, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x^2} = \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nbut for cube roots, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{x^3} = x\n$$\n\nNo absolute value is needed for cube roots, because\n\n- the cube root of a positive number is a positive number, and\n- the cube root of a negative number is a negative number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069942 #edb/ref 1065 1605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069942 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ad1bc727-9054-5115-83f0-a82aa24dc35e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069942 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
